  "details": "This seems like a fairly low security risk feature to add and I don't know why it's not already available.\nSo this problem probably goes for other text inputs as well but I specifically am having an issue where I want a VRCInputField to prepend text in front of whatever a user is going to input into a video player, but by default the caret position starts at the front of the prepended text. This causes an issue where they either need to double click and set the caret position at the end of the prepended text or they need to type a bunch of randomness until the caret position is at the end of the prepended text to then begin typing in the link they want. \nThe only reason why I see this as an issue is because I want the prepended text to be done behind the scenes, meaning I'm using a second text field so that they only see what they type in the input field and don't see the prepended text. That means they would have no idea that they have to click in front of the prepended text or type a bunch of randomness to get the caret position right before adding the link they want",
